  "summary": "The Oaklandside provides an FAQ-style explainer on Flock Safety's automated license plate readers in Oakland, describing how the cameras work, how OPD came to deploy nearly 300 of them, and the arguments for and against. It covers privacy concerns, reported misuse for abortion and immigration enforcement investigations, and mixed academic evidence on crime reduction.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Oakland currently has 293 Flock cameras installed throughout the city, according to the city's Flock transparency portal.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "Multiple cities nationwide have terminated their contracts with Flock, limited data sharing and access, or imposed hefty fines for contract violations, due to privacy and security concerns.",
      "paragraph_idx": 26
    },
    {
      "quote": "an officer with the Johnson County Sheriff's Office accessed over 80,000 license plate records from Texas, Washington, and Illinois to try to locate a woman whom authorities said had a 'self-administered abortion.'",
      "paragraph_idx": 28
    }
  ],
